# TVsham website: rewrites and refusals for Netlify (Cloudflare Pages reads the 200 rules too, and
# ignores 404 rules: there, publish only the build output, which holds nothing below but these
# hosting files, and Cloudflare does not serve _headers or _redirects in any case).
#
# The app is one page with four routes. A visit or a reload at a route's address gets the page,
# which then draws that route; every other missing address gets 404.html with a 404, rather than
# the app with a 200, so a mistyped address and a missing script both say what they are.
/settings   /index.html  200
/library    /index.html  200
/result     /index.html  200

# The hosting files are not part of the site.
/_headers    /404.html  404
/_redirects  /404.html  404
/.htaccess   /404.html  404
